# Copy this file to .env in this same folder and fill in real values.
# .env is gitignored by the repo root .gitignore (.env / .env.*); this file
# (.env.example) is checked in as documentation only — never put real secrets here.
# After editing .env, reload the window (Command Palette > Developer: Reload Window)
# so the extension picks it up.

# Google's OAuth token endpoint requires a client_secret for the Antigravity IDE's
# OAuth client even though it's a public "Desktop app" client — the redirect-URI +
# PKCE flow is the real security boundary, not this value's confidentiality (Google's
# own docs say so; every community Antigravity-auth proxy ships this exact value in
# plaintext: NoeFabris/opencode-antigravity-auth, shekohex/opencode-google-antigravity-auth,
# KashifKhn/gemini-proxy). Only needed if you use the "Google Antigravity" provider's
# Sign In button.
ANTIGRAVITY_CLIENT_SECRET=
